INSERT INTO company_dossiers (ticker,status,description,lede,sells,revenue_model,opportunity,must_go_right,editor_note,bull_title,bull_json,bear_title,bear_json,thesis_breaker,financial_drivers_json,risks_json,monitor_json,questions_json,competitors,evidence_date,validated_at,published_at,updated_at) VALUES
('AUR','published','Autonomous-driving technology company commercializing driverless systems for freight transportation.','Aurora develops the Aurora Driver and a driver-as-a-service model for autonomous trucks, with longer-term applicability to ride-hailing vehicles. Safety performance, route expansion, fleet utilization, partner execution, unit economics, cash runway and dilution drive value.','Autonomous-driving software, sensors, compute, fleet-support systems and driver-as-a-service for commercial trucking.','Potential per-mile or service revenue from autonomous freight operations, supported by vehicle, logistics, manufacturing and fleet-service partners.','Driverless trucking can increase asset utilization, address driver constraints and improve safety or operating consistency on suitable routes.','Aurora must prove safe operation without a driver, scale hardware and remote support, integrate with trucks, satisfy regulators and customers, and reach positive unit economics before cash is exhausted.','Commercial miles are not sufficient alone. Track driverless miles, safety events, intervention and assistance rates, route domain, fleet availability, paid loads, revenue per mile, support cost, hardware cost, cash burn and diluted shares.','A validated driverless service could scale across a large freight market','["Trucking offers repetitive highway routes and measurable customer economics.","A common driver platform can leverage vehicle and logistics partnerships.","Successful safety evidence can create data and deployment advantages."]','Safety, scaling and financing risks remain existential','["A serious incident could halt deployment and damage regulatory trust.","Prototype success may not translate into reliable fleet economics.","Long development and hardware cycles can require substantial dilution."]','The thesis breaks if Aurora cannot demonstrate safe, repeatable and economically positive driverless freight before financing materially erodes per-share value','[{"label":"SAFETY CASE","value":"Permission to scale","detail":"Driverless miles, events, interventions, domain and independent evidence"},{"label":"FLEET ECONOMICS","value":"Commercial proof","detail":"Paid loads, utilization, revenue per mile, support and hardware cost"},{"label":"RUNWAY / SCALE","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Fleet additions, partner commitments, cash burn and diluted shares"}]','[{"title":"Safety and regulation","level":"High","text":"Autonomous operation can cause physical harm and regulatory shutdown.","signal":"Incidents, recalls, disengagement, investigations and route limits"},{"title":"Technical scale","level":"High","text":"Edge cases, weather and fleet reliability may resist commercial scaling.","signal":"Assistance rate, uptime, route expansion and maintenance"},{"title":"Financing and concentration","level":"High","text":"Long timelines and dependence on a few partners increase capital risk.","signal":"Runway, commitments, offerings and share count"}]','[{"title":"Driverless operating cohort","text":"Track safety, utilization and cost for each route and fleet generation.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Per-mile cash bridge","text":"Require paid revenue to exceed vehicle, remote support, insurance and maintenance cost.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["What independent evidence supports safe driverless expansion beyond the current operating domain?","When does a truck produce positive contribution after all support and hardware costs?","How much deployment can current cash fund on a fully diluted basis?"]','Kodiak, Torc, Waabi, traditional carriers and other autonomous-trucking developers.','2026-02-11','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AURA','published','Clinical-stage biotechnology company developing targeted oncology therapies for ocular and urologic cancers.','Aura Biosciences advances a virus-like drug-conjugate platform led by bel-sar, with programs intended to treat tumors while preserving affected organs. Randomized efficacy, durability, vision or organ outcomes, safety, regulatory alignment, manufacturing and runway drive value.','Investigational targeted oncology therapies, including bel-sar for ocular and urologic cancer settings.','Before approval, value depends on research funding, collaborations and external capital; successful therapies could generate product, licensing, milestone or royalty revenue.','Organ-preserving treatment could address patients who otherwise face invasive procedures or loss of function.','Aura must show clinically meaningful tumor control, durable organ preservation, manageable safety, scalable manufacturing and regulator-agreed endpoints in controlled trials.','Enrollment is not evidence. Track protocol, control arm, tumor response, recurrence, metastasis, visual or organ function, adverse events, dosing, manufacturing comparability, cash runway and diluted shares.','Organ-preserving oncology could create differentiated clinical value','["Targeted delivery may concentrate treatment at the tumor.","Preserving vision or organ function is a meaningful patient outcome.","A platform may support more than one tumor setting if biology transfers."]','Clinical, endpoint and financing risks remain binary','["Local tumor response may not translate into durable disease control.","Small or open-label studies can overstate efficacy and safety.","Pivotal trials and manufacturing can consume substantial capital before approval."]','The thesis breaks if controlled trials fail to show durable tumor control and functional benefit sufficient to outweigh safety and treatment burden','[{"label":"CONTROLLED EFFICACY","value":"Clinical proof","detail":"Response, recurrence, metastasis, control comparison and missing data"},{"label":"FUNCTION / SAFETY","value":"Patient value","detail":"Vision or organ preservation, adverse events, dosing and procedures"},{"label":"RUNWAY / SCALE","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Enrollment, manufacturing, regulatory milestones, burn and diluted shares"}]','[{"title":"Clinical interpretation","level":"High","text":"Surrogate or local responses may not predict durable patient benefit.","signal":"Randomized results, follow-up and recurrence"},{"title":"Safety and manufacturing","level":"High","text":"Targeted biologic products require consistent production and local tolerability.","signal":"Serious events, discontinuations, batch comparability and holds"},{"title":"Financing","level":"High","text":"Pivotal programs can require external capital before decisive results.","signal":"Runway, trial cost, offerings and share count"}]','[{"title":"Pivotal evidence audit","text":"Evaluate complete randomized data, follow-up and function-preserving outcomes.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Runway to readout","text":"Compare cash and enrollment pace with remaining trial and manufacturing cost.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["What endpoint establishes benefit beyond local tumor response?","How durable are control and organ-preserving outcomes?","Can current capital fund the decisive trial and required manufacturing work?"]','Radiation, surgery, intravesical therapies and other ocular or urologic oncology developers.','2026-03-30','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVA','published','Regulated electric and natural-gas utility serving customers in the northwestern United States and Alaska.','Avista invests in generation, transmission, distribution and gas infrastructure and recovers approved costs through regulated rates. Rate-base growth, regulatory outcomes, load, financing cost, wildfire exposure, reliability and per-share cash needs drive value.','Electric generation and delivery, natural-gas distribution and related regulated utility services.','Customer rates approved by state regulators are intended to recover prudent operating costs, depreciation and financing while providing an allowed return on invested capital.','Grid modernization, clean generation and replacement of aging infrastructure can support regulated investment and earnings growth.','Avista must obtain timely rate recovery, execute capital projects, maintain reliability, manage wildfire and fuel risks, and finance growth without excessive customer pressure or dilution.','Rate-base growth is not automatically value creation. Track allowed versus earned return, regulatory lag, customer bills, load, capital plan, wildfire mitigation, debt, interest, equity issuance and operating cash.','Constructive regulation can support visible infrastructure returns','["Essential service demand provides recurring regulated revenue.","Approved investment can expand rate base over long asset lives.","Hydro and diversified infrastructure can support regional reliability."]','Regulatory lag and financing can dilute rate-base growth','["Regulators may disallow costs or delay recovery.","Wildfire, storms and outages can create large liabilities and capital needs.","High interest and equity issuance can reduce per-share earnings from investment."]','The thesis breaks if earned returns remain below the cost of capital while wildfire and financing needs cause persistent per-share dilution','[{"label":"REGULATORY RETURN","value":"Earning quality","detail":"Allowed and earned ROE, rate cases, lag, disallowance and affordability"},{"label":"CAPITAL / RELIABILITY","value":"Operating proof","detail":"Project cost, load, outages, wildfire mitigation and asset performance"},{"label":"FINANCING / SHARE","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Operating cash, debt, interest, equity issuance, dividend and EPS"}]','[{"title":"Regulatory and affordability","level":"High","text":"Customer-bill pressure can limit timely recovery of investment and cost.","signal":"Rate orders, settlements, lag and disallowance"},{"title":"Wildfire and operations","level":"High","text":"Fire, weather and infrastructure failure can harm communities and create liability.","signal":"Incidents, mitigation, insurance and reserves"},{"title":"Capital and interest rates","level":"High","text":"Large investment programs require continuing debt and equity funding.","signal":"Credit metrics, interest, issuance and dividend coverage"}]','[{"title":"Rate-case scorecard","text":"Compare requested and approved revenue, return and recovery timing by jurisdiction.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Per-share financing","text":"Reconcile rate-base growth with debt, equity issuance and dividend cash needs.","impact":"BULL CASE"}]','["Is earned return converging toward the authorized level?","Which wildfire costs are insured or recoverable from customers?","Can operating cash and debt capacity fund the plan without persistent equity dilution?"]','Northwestern regulated electric and gas utilities, public power and alternative energy suppliers.','2026-02-25','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVAH','published','Home-healthcare provider serving medically complex children, adults and older patients across the United States.','Aveanna provides private-duty nursing, home health, hospice and medical solutions. Clinician availability, reimbursed hours or visits, wage-rate matching, payer mix, acquisitions, leverage, quality and cash conversion drive value.','Private-duty nursing, home health and hospice visits, therapy, enteral nutrition and other home-based medical services.','Reimbursement from Medicaid, Medicare, managed-care plans and other payers based on authorized hours, visits, episodes, products or contracted services.','Aging populations and preference for lower-cost home care can expand demand if reimbursement supports a stable clinical workforce.','Aveanna must recruit and retain nurses, obtain authorizations, deliver compliant care, secure rate increases, integrate acquisitions and reduce leverage while maintaining quality.','Demand is not served revenue without staff. Track authorized versus staffed hours, admissions, visits, clinician turnover, wage-rate spread, payer mix, denials, quality, acquisitions, debt and free cash flow.','Home-based care demand can support scaled recurring services','["Care at home can be preferred by patients and less costly than institutional settings.","A national platform can support payer relationships and recruiting infrastructure.","Reimbursement improvement can unlock previously unstaffed demand."]','Labor, reimbursement and leverage can overwhelm demand','["Nurse shortages can leave authorized hours unfilled.","Government and managed-care rates may lag wage inflation.","Debt and acquisition integration can absorb operating progress."]','The thesis breaks if reimbursement and staffing fail to produce sustained cash flow sufficient to reduce leverage and fund quality care','[{"label":"STAFFED CARE","value":"Demand conversion","detail":"Authorized and staffed hours, visits, admissions, census and clinician retention"},{"label":"RATE / WAGE","value":"Unit economics","detail":"Reimbursement, wage, overtime, mix, denials and segment margin"},{"label":"CASH / LEVERAGE","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Working capital, acquisitions, interest, debt paydown and free cash flow"}]','[{"title":"Clinical labor","level":"High","text":"Shortages and turnover constrain service capacity and raise wages.","signal":"Open shifts, overtime, turnover and unstaffed hours"},{"title":"Reimbursement and compliance","level":"High","text":"Public payers set rates and require detailed authorization and documentation.","signal":"Rate actions, denials, audits and recoupments"},{"title":"Leverage and acquisition","level":"High","text":"Debt and purchased growth increase fixed claims and integration demands.","signal":"Interest, covenant headroom, synergies and cash flow"}]','[{"title":"Authorization-to-service bridge","text":"Measure how much approved care becomes staffed, billed and collected revenue.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Debt reduction","text":"Require operating improvement to convert into sustained net debt decline.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["What percentage of authorized private-duty hours is currently staffed?","Are payer-rate increases exceeding wage and overtime inflation?","How quickly can free cash flow reduce debt after acquisition spending?"]','BrightSpring, Addus, Enhabit, home-health agencies and local private-duty nursing providers.','2026-03-19','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVAV','published','Defense-technology company providing autonomous systems, loitering munitions, space, cyber and directed-energy capabilities.','AeroVironment combines unmanned aircraft and precision-strike systems with expanded space, cyber and directed-energy operations. Funded orders, program execution, government budgets, integration, fixed-price risk, accounting quality and free cash flow drive value.','Uncrewed aircraft, loitering munitions, counter-UAS systems, space platforms, directed-energy, cyber and electronic-warfare products and services.','Product deliveries, development and service contracts with U.S. and allied government customers, under fixed-price, cost-reimbursement and other contractual structures.','Demand for autonomous, attritable and counter-drone systems can expand as defense customers modernize for contested environments.','AeroVironment must win funded programs, scale production, meet mission and delivery requirements, integrate acquired businesses and convert backlog into margin and cash.','Awards and indefinite contracts are not funded revenue. Track funded backlog, orders, delivery schedules, contract type, program margin, cost revisions, inventory, receivables, acquisition accounting, debt and diluted shares.','Mission-proven systems can earn expanding defense-program positions','["Operational use can validate products and accelerate follow-on demand.","A broader capability set can support integrated customer solutions.","Rising autonomous and counter-UAS priorities can create sustained budgets."]','Program, integration and accounting risk can erode backlog value','["Defense awards can be protested, delayed, reduced or unfunded.","Fixed-price development and rapid production can create cost overruns.","Large acquisitions increase integration, goodwill, leverage and reporting complexity."]','The thesis breaks if funded backlog and acquired capabilities fail to produce sustainable free cash flow and per-share returns after full integration cost','[{"label":"FUNDED DEMAND","value":"Revenue visibility","detail":"Funded backlog, orders, appropriations, deliveries and customer acceptance"},{"label":"PROGRAM MARGIN","value":"Execution proof","detail":"Contract type, cost revisions, production yield, mix and segment margin"},{"label":"INTEGRATION / CASH","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Synergies, goodwill, debt, working capital, capex and diluted shares"}]','[{"title":"Government programs","level":"High","text":"Budgets, priorities, protests and customer acceptance affect timing and value.","signal":"Funding, modifications, cancellations and awards"},{"title":"Fixed-price execution","level":"High","text":"Development or production cost can exceed contract assumptions.","signal":"Charges, estimate changes, yield and late deliveries"},{"title":"Integration and reporting","level":"High","text":"Acquisitions add systems, culture, goodwill and accounting risk.","signal":"Control findings, impairment, synergies and cash conversion"}]','[{"title":"Award-to-cash bridge","text":"Track each large program from funded order through accepted delivery and cash collection.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Acquisition return","text":"Compare incremental cash profit with purchase price, debt, shares and integration spending.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["How much backlog is funded and scheduled for delivery?","Which programs carry the greatest fixed-price or development risk?","Do acquired capabilities increase free cash flow per diluted share after integration?"]','Anduril, General Atomics, Northrop Grumman, RTX, L3Harris and other autonomous or defense-system suppliers.','2026-06-29','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVBC','published','Bank holding company for Avidia Bank, a Massachusetts community bank that completed a mutual-to-stock conversion.','Avidia Bancorp earns spread and fee income from relationship loans, deposits and payment-related banking services. Deposit quality, net interest margin, credit, conversion capital, growth discipline and per-share capital allocation drive value.','Commercial, residential and consumer loans, deposits, treasury and payment services, and other community-banking products.','Net interest income from loans and securities funded by deposits, plus service, interchange, payment and other fee income.','Fresh conversion capital can support prudent growth, technology and capital returns if management avoids weak credit or uneconomic expansion.','Avidia must retain core deposits, price loans through rate cycles, protect asset quality and deploy excess capital without chasing volume or overpaying for acquisitions.','Conversion equity is not earning power. Track tangible book value, core and uninsured deposits, deposit beta, loan mix, margin, criticized assets, charge-offs, securities marks, capital deployment and shares.','Core deposits plus conversion capital can support measured compounding','["A local franchise can build sticky relationship deposits.","New capital provides a buffer against credit and rate shocks.","Disciplined deployment can grow tangible value per share."]','Excess capital can encourage poor underwriting or allocation','["Deposit competition can compress margin.","Commercial or real-estate concentrations can create correlated losses.","Rapid growth, acquisitions or mistimed buybacks can waste conversion capital."]','The thesis breaks if management deploys conversion capital at returns below the cost of equity and tangible book value per share fails to compound','[{"label":"DEPOSIT FRANCHISE","value":"Funding quality","detail":"Core mix, uninsured deposits, cost, beta and retention"},{"label":"CREDIT / MARGIN","value":"Earning quality","detail":"Loan mix, net interest margin, criticized assets, losses and reserves"},{"label":"CAPITAL DEPLOYMENT","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Tangible book, growth, acquisitions, dividends, repurchases and shares"}]','[{"title":"Rate and deposit competition","level":"High","text":"Funding can reprice faster than loans and securities.","signal":"Deposit beta, mix, wholesale funding and margin"},{"title":"Credit concentration","level":"High","text":"Community-bank real-estate and commercial exposures can correlate.","signal":"Criticized assets, nonperformers and charge-offs"},{"title":"Capital allocation","level":"High","text":"New conversion capital may be deployed at inadequate returns.","signal":"Loan pricing, deal multiples, buyback price and tangible book"}]','[{"title":"Conversion-capital scorecard","text":"Track cumulative earnings and capital actions against tangible book value per share.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Deposit cohorts","text":"Measure retention and pricing of operating versus rate-sensitive deposits.","impact":"BULL CASE"}]','["What portion of deposits represents durable customer operating balances?","Where can the bank deploy capital without weakening underwriting?","Are repurchases or acquisitions accretive to conservative tangible value per share?"]','Massachusetts community and regional banks, credit unions and national banks.','2026-03-27','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVBH','published','Business-bank holding company serving commercial clients in Silicon Valley and broader specialty lending markets.','Avidbank focuses on commercial and industrial, commercial real-estate, construction, venture, asset-based and sponsor-finance relationships. Deposit concentration, margin, credit selection, technology-cycle exposure, liquidity and capital drive owner value.','Commercial loans, venture and sponsor finance, construction and real-estate credit, deposits, treasury management and personal banking.','Net interest income from loans and securities funded by deposits, plus treasury and other banking fees.','Specialized bankers can earn attractive relationships in complex niches underserved by standardized national-bank processes.','Avidbank must maintain disciplined underwriting, diversify funding, retain relationship deposits and manage concentrated venture, construction and commercial exposures through cycles.','Growth can hide concentration. Track industry and borrower mix, unfunded commitments, criticized loans, nonperformers, deposits by type and size, uninsured share, wholesale funding, margin, capital and tangible book.','Specialized relationships can support attractive risk-adjusted spreads','["Experienced niche teams can price and structure complex credit.","Treasury relationships can bring valuable operating deposits.","A focused platform can respond faster than larger banks."]','Funding and credit concentration can change quickly','["Large uninsured or venture-related deposits may be volatile.","Construction, commercial real estate and sponsor loans can correlate in downturns.","Rapid niche growth can weaken underwriting before losses appear."]','The thesis breaks if concentrated funding or credit losses cause lasting damage to tangible common equity and per-share earning power','[{"label":"FUNDING STABILITY","value":"Liquidity proof","detail":"Operating and uninsured deposits, concentration, beta and wholesale funding"},{"label":"CREDIT COHORTS","value":"Underwriting proof","detail":"Industry, vintage, collateral, criticized assets, losses and reserves"},{"label":"CAPITAL / BOOK","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Margin, operating leverage, tangible equity, capital ratios and shares"}]','[{"title":"Deposit concentration","level":"High","text":"Commercial and venture clients may move large balances rapidly.","signal":"Top depositors, uninsured mix, outflow and liquidity"},{"title":"Specialty credit","level":"High","text":"Venture, construction and sponsor loans can be cyclic and difficult to value.","signal":"Criticized loans, collateral, extensions and charge-offs"},{"title":"Regional and technology cycle","level":"Medium","text":"Silicon Valley conditions can affect borrowers and deposits together.","signal":"Funding markets, layoffs, vacancies and client formation"}]','[{"title":"Liquidity stress test","text":"Compare available liquidity with concentrated uninsured-deposit outflow scenarios.","impact":"BEAR CASE"},{"title":"Vintage credit audit","text":"Track growth cohorts from origination through criticized status and loss.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["How concentrated are uninsured deposits among the largest relationships?","Which loan niches produce returns after normalized losses?","Does growth compound tangible book value without increasing tail risk?"]','Silicon Valley Bank, regional business banks, private credit and specialty finance providers.','2026-03-18','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVBP','published','Clinical-stage biotechnology company developing and licensing oncology therapies from global innovation hubs.','ArriVent advances targeted cancer medicines led by firmonertinib for EGFR-mutated non-small-cell lung cancer. Randomized efficacy, central-nervous-system activity, resistance coverage, safety, licensed rights, regulatory execution and runway drive value.','Investigational targeted oncology drugs, including firmonertinib and additional in-licensed development programs.','Before approval, economics depend on collaboration and licensing terms, milestones and external capital; approved products could generate sales, royalties or partnered revenue.','A differentiated EGFR therapy could serve patients with uncommon mutations, brain metastases or resistance not fully addressed by existing drugs.','ArriVent must show clinically meaningful and durable benefit against appropriate controls, manage toxicity, preserve licensed rights, scale supply and fund pivotal development.','Response rate alone is incomplete. Track randomized progression-free and overall survival, response duration, CNS outcomes, mutation subgroups, adverse events, dose changes, enrollment, milestone obligations, runway and diluted shares.','Differentiated mutation coverage could support meaningful oncology value','["Precision selection can concentrate treatment benefit in defined patients.","Global licensing can access programs beyond traditional discovery networks.","CNS activity and uncommon-mutation coverage may create differentiation."]','Clinical and licensed-asset concentration remain high','["Promising single-arm responses may not outperform standard therapy.","Safety or resistance can limit dosing and durability.","Milestone, royalty and territory obligations reduce retained economics."]','The thesis breaks if controlled trials fail to show differentiated durable benefit after accounting for safety and all licensing obligations','[{"label":"RANDOMIZED BENEFIT","value":"Clinical proof","detail":"PFS, OS, response duration, control comparison and subgroup consistency"},{"label":"CNS / SAFETY","value":"Differentiation","detail":"Brain response, adverse events, dose intensity and discontinuation"},{"label":"RIGHTS / RUNWAY","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Territories, milestones, royalties, supply, burn and diluted shares"}]','[{"title":"Clinical efficacy","level":"High","text":"Early responses may not translate into randomized survival benefit.","signal":"Control results, durability, censoring and independent review"},{"title":"Safety and resistance","level":"High","text":"Toxicity or emerging resistance can narrow use.","signal":"Grade events, dose changes, discontinuation and progression biology"},{"title":"Licensing and financing","level":"High","text":"Third-party rights and long trials limit retained value and require capital.","signal":"Milestones, royalties, runway and offerings"}]','[{"title":"Trial evidence table","text":"Audit every endpoint, control, subgroup and follow-up period from the pivotal program.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Retained-value bridge","text":"Subtract milestones, royalties, development cost and dilution from product economics.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["What outcome would establish superiority or a distinct line of therapy?","How consistent are CNS and uncommon-mutation results across cohorts?","What economics remain after all licensing, development and financing obligations?"]','AstraZeneca, Johnson & Johnson, Blueprint Medicines and other EGFR-targeted oncology developers.','2026-03-05','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVEX','published','Defense-technology company providing autonomous unmanned systems, precision-strike products and adaptable mission solutions.','AEVEX develops and delivers unmanned aircraft, autonomy and mission systems for U.S. and allied defense customers. Funded programs, production scale, contract mix, customer concentration, mission reliability, public-company capital structure and free cash flow drive value.','Autonomous unmanned aircraft, precision-strike systems, mission payloads, intelligence support and related engineering or operational services.','Product deliveries and government program revenue under fixed-price, cost-reimbursement and service contracts, with timing driven by funding, milestones and acceptance.','Demand for attritable autonomous systems and rapid defense procurement can expand production and follow-on programs.','AEVEX must convert prototype and urgent demand into funded repeat programs, scale manufacturing, meet mission and quality requirements and control fixed-price and acquisition-related costs.','The June 2026 S-1 is the current annual primary filing because AEVEX has not yet filed a Form 10-K. Track funded backlog, contract type, customer mix, delivery acceptance, production yield, program margin, working capital, debt and diluted shares.','Rapidly deployable autonomous systems can win repeat defense demand','["Modern conflicts increase demand for attritable autonomous capability.","Operational feedback can accelerate product iteration and follow-on orders.","Integrated mission systems can deepen customer relationships."]','Newly public, concentrated and contract-sensitive economics remain risky','["A small number of defense programs and customers may drive results.","Fixed-price production or development can create large overruns.","IPO and sponsor ownership, debt and acquisitions complicate per-share economics."]','The thesis breaks if funded programs do not convert into reliable production margin and free cash flow after public-company and capital-structure costs','[{"label":"FUNDED PROGRAMS","value":"Demand proof","detail":"Awards, appropriations, backlog, option exercise, deliveries and acceptance"},{"label":"PRODUCTION MARGIN","value":"Execution proof","detail":"Contract type, yield, suppliers, cost revisions, mix and warranty"},{"label":"CAPITAL STRUCTURE","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Sponsor ownership, debt, IPO shares, stock compensation and cash"}]','[{"title":"Customer and program concentration","level":"High","text":"Government priorities and a few contracts can change revenue quickly.","signal":"Top programs, funding, options and cancellations"},{"title":"Fixed-price and manufacturing","level":"High","text":"Rapid scaling can produce cost overruns, quality problems and delays.","signal":"Estimate changes, yield, late delivery and charges"},{"title":"New-public-company structure","level":"High","text":"Sponsor rights, debt, acquisitions and controls affect common owners.","signal":"Related parties, dilution, debt, control findings and cash conversion"}]','[{"title":"Contract ledger","text":"Track each material program from funded award through accepted delivery and cash.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Post-IPO per-share audit","text":"Reconcile operating results with debt, sponsor interests, stock compensation and diluted shares.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["How much backlog is funded and non-cancellable?","Which programs carry the greatest production or fixed-price risk?","What free cash flow belongs to common owners after debt and dilution?"]','AeroVironment, Anduril, Kratos, L3Harris and other autonomous defense-system suppliers.','2026-06-01','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('AVIR','published','Late-stage clinical biotechnology company developing oral antiviral therapies for serious RNA-virus infections.','Atea Pharmaceuticals advances a regimen of bemnifosbuvir and ruzasvir for hepatitis C and an earlier hepatitis E program. Phase 3 cure rates, control comparison, resistance, safety, drug interactions, commercial differentiation, runway and strategic alternatives drive value.','Investigational oral antiviral combinations and nucleotide-prodrug candidates for hepatitis C, hepatitis E and potential additional viruses.','Before approval, economics depend on collaborations, licensing and external capital; successful regimens could generate product sales, milestones or royalties.','A short, broadly effective and convenient oral regimen could improve test-and-treat access and address gaps in current hepatitis care.','Atea must show high sustained virologic response across difficult subgroups, acceptable safety and interactions, resistance coverage, regulator-aligned manufacturing and competitive commercial value.','Topline cure rate needs context. Track SVR12 denominator, missing data, cirrhosis, genotype, prior treatment, resistance, relapse, adverse events, discontinuation, interactions, comparator, runway and diluted shares.','A competitive oral regimen could address persistent global treatment gaps','["Hepatitis C remains curable but underdiagnosed and undertreated.","Complementary antiviral mechanisms may provide high barrier to resistance.","A nucleotide platform can support additional RNA-virus programs."]','Phase 3, competition and capital risk remain binary','["Established regimens already achieve high cure rates.","Small differences in efficacy, safety or interactions can determine adoption.","Failed or undifferentiated trials can leave limited pipeline value after burn."]','The thesis breaks if Phase 3 results do not demonstrate a clinically and commercially differentiated benefit with feasible retained economics','[{"label":"SVR12 EVIDENCE","value":"Clinical proof","detail":"Denominator, comparator, genotype, cirrhosis, missing data and relapse"},{"label":"PROFILE","value":"Differentiation","detail":"Safety, interactions, resistance, duration, pill burden and subgroups"},{"label":"RUNWAY / STRATEGY","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Cash burn, launch needs, partnerships, alternatives and diluted shares"}]','[{"title":"Clinical differentiation","level":"High","text":"Very effective incumbents leave little tolerance for inferior results.","signal":"SVR12, subgroup consistency, safety and interactions"},{"title":"Regulatory and manufacturing","level":"High","text":"Combination products require consistent supply and aligned evidence.","signal":"FDA feedback, CMC, inspections and filing timing"},{"title":"Financing and strategic execution","level":"High","text":"Launch or further trials may require partners or substantial capital.","signal":"Runway, advisory process, deals and share count"}]','[{"title":"Phase 3 denominator audit","text":"Recalculate cure rates including every randomized patient and missing outcome.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Commercial hurdle","text":"Compare regimen duration, safety, interactions and net economics with incumbents.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["Does Phase 3 efficacy remain competitive across difficult patient subgroups?","Which safety or interaction features change physician choice?","What partnership or capital is required to file and commercialize the regimen?"]','Gilead Sciences, AbbVie, Merck and other antiviral developers or established hepatitis regimens.','2026-03-05','2026-08-05T17:10:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
